<title>USA: Guilford Mills sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Guilford Mills sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, N.C. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guilford Mills Inc said Monday that its board of directors has approved a 3-for-2 stock split of the company's common stock.</p>
<p>The split, said the company, will be in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend, payable on May 12 to stockholders of record, May 1.</p>
<p>As a result, stockholders will receive one new share for each two shares owned on May 1, said the company. Shareholders will receive cash in lieu of fractional shares in accordance with the closing price on the record date.</p>
</text>
